I'd also add that in designing any new anything, it's best to have a
good, solid foundation in how the game mechanics work, and what a
reasonably optimal strategy for each role would be to ascend
no-holds-barred in a relatively short timespan.

Any character can ascend in 100,000 turns by endlessly overpreparing,
farming, whatever.  But to turn limited resources into a 20,000 turn
ascension requires leaning heavily on the most powerful resources
available, and a strong knowledge of exactly what does and doesn't work
in any given situation.  This ain't exactly trivial.

